[-] conclave		<-->	n++[--0]	./ˈkɒŋkleɪv/
 /ˈkɑːnkleɪv/
(formal)
	;mật nghị -- (1) ​a meeting to discuss something in private; the people at this meeting
		;Word Origin
	;;

























[-] void		<-->	n++[--0]	./vɔɪd/
 /vɔɪd/
[usually singular] (formal or literary)
	;khoảng không -- (1) a large empty space
		;Below him was nothing but a black void.
		;She sat staring into the void, emptying her mind of all thoughts.
				;Oxford Collocations Dictionary
				;adjective
				;bigdeepgreat…
				;verb + void
				;createleavefill…
		;See full entry
	;cảm giác trống vắng -- (2) a feeling of being empty, caused by the loss of somebody/something
		;The void left by his mother's death was never filled.
		;It seemed that nothing could fill the aching black void left by Rachel’s death.
		;Word Origin
	;;












[-] candid		<-->	a++[0]	./ˈkændɪd/
 /ˈkændɪd/
	;thành thật, chân thành -- (1) saying what you think openly and honestly; not hiding your thoughts
		;a candid statement/interview
		;I felt she was being less than candid with me.
		;To be candid, I can’t stand her.
		;The ex-minister gave a candid interview about his reasons for resigning.
		;see also candour
				;Oxford Collocations Dictionary
				;verbs
				;be
				;adverb
				;verydisarminglyrefreshingly…
				;preposition
				;aboutwith
		;See full entry
	; -- (2) a candid photograph is one that is taken without the person in it knowing that they are being photographed
		;He mingled among the guests and took the candid shots which were much more fun than the formal group photographs.
		;Word Origin
	;;












